# tally 2.3.1 rulings 14 B5, 17 B (G1's review, f12): a `same` group of two decisions (in1, in2) or a plan and
# a decision (j1, j2) on two days is one movement: the hole from the first day, booked from the later
# decision's point with its amount where they agree (b8, c8 100.00 PLN). Before: b6 100.00 PLN, b8 and c8
# the HOLE-SAME hole for good.
=== f12_dec_sides_min.tally
model f12
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "probe"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place wallet: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place w2: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place other: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a: money PLN
input d1: date
input d2: date
move in1: transfers
  reads other
  on d1
  leg cash from world to wallet amount a + 0 * bal(other)
move in2: transfers
  reads other
  on d2
  leg cash from world to wallet amount a + 0 * bal(other)
move j1: transfers
  on d1
  leg cash from world to w2 amount a
move j2: transfers
  reads other
  on d2
  leg cash from world to w2 amount a + 0 * bal(other)
ask b6: bal(wallet, 2026-03-06)
ask b8: bal(wallet, 2026-03-08)
ask c6: bal(w2, 2026-03-06)
ask c8: bal(w2, 2026-03-08)
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  opening[wallet] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[w2] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[other] = 5.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  a = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d1 = 2026-03-05 "s"
  d2 = 2026-03-07 "s"
  same in1 = in2
  same j1 = j2
=== expect
b6: ?"in1 and in2 are one, but the leg at wallet differs on 2026-03-05: 100.00 PLN (in1) and its day 2026-03-07 (in2)" (in1, in2)
  unfulfilled: in1
  cut 2026-06-10
b8: 100.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: in1
  unfulfilled: in2
  cut 2026-06-10
c6: ?"j1 and j2 are one, but the leg at w2 differs on 2026-03-05: 100.00 PLN (j1) and its day 2026-03-07 (j2)" (j1, j2)
  unfulfilled: j1
  cut 2026-06-10
c8: 100.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: j1
  unfulfilled: j2
  cut 2026-06-10
